          "content": "# Data & datasets\n\nThe unsexy half of frontier model training. Where training data comes from, what it gets filtered for, and why dataset choices show up in model behavior.\n\n## The data pipeline\n\n*(crawl → filter → dedup → mix → tokenize; orders of magnitude shrink at each step)*\n\n## Sources\n\n*(Common Crawl, code (GitHub, Software Heritage), books, papers (arXiv, S2ORC), Q&A (StackExchange), Wikipedia, synthetic)*\n\n## What pretraining mixes look like\n\n*(public-disclosure mixes from OLMo, Llama, DeepSeek; what's known about closed-lab mixes)*\n\n## Synthetic data\n\n*(distillation traces, self-instruct, persona generation; why it's eating real data; risks of model collapse)*\n\n## Dataset cards & provenance\n\n*(why labs publish them, what to look for; the gap between \"card\" and \"actual contents\")*\n\n## Licensing & legal\n\n*(copyright, fair-use posture, opt-out signals like robots.txt and ai.txt; ongoing lawsuits)*\n\n## Resources\n\n- [The Pile paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.00027)\n- [Dolma (AI2)](https://allenai.org/dolma)\n- [RedPajama](https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data)\n\n## Notes\n\n*(stub — replace with study content)*"
